     against the report before proceeding.
  3. [1mTask review[0m — a separate reviewer subagent gets the brief, the report, and a generated diff package. It returns two
     verdicts: spec compliance and code quality. Both are required.
  4. [1mFix loop if needed[0m — capped at five rounds per task. Rounds 1-3 resume the original implementer; rounds 4-5
     dispatch a fresh implementer on a more capable model. Each round ends in a scoped re-review of just the fix diff.
     Minor findings get deferred to the ledger instead of entering the loop.
  5. [1mCodex gate[0m — under Claude Code, an optional second-opinion review runs per task (skipped for tasks declared
     low-risk whose plan was itself gate-reviewed). Degrades cleanly to a no-op if Codex isn't installed. Its rounds
     share the same five-round budget.
  6. [1mLedger the completion[0m, move on.

  [1mEnd of run[0m

  One broad whole-branch review on the most capable model, pointed at the deferred-minors list. If it finds things:
  exactly [1mone[0m fix dispatch carrying the whole findings list (not one fixer per finding — that's expensive), then one
  scoped re-review. Residuals get surfaced to you as BLOCKED rather than looped on. Then the scratch workspace is
  deleted and it hands off to [38;5;153mfinishing-a-development-branch[39m.

  [1mWhat it asks of you[0m

  It runs [1mcontinuously[0m — no "should I continue?" between tasks. It stops only for: a blocker it can't resolve, a review
  finding that conflicts with what the plan itself mandates (you decide which governs), or completion.

  [1mWhen it's the wrong tool[0m

  - No plan yet → brainstorm and write one first.
  - Tasks tightly coupled with shared state → sequential inline execution is safer.
  - You want a separate session / human-in-the-loop per task → [38;5;153mexecuting-plans[39m instead.

  ---

  One relevant note: your global CLAUDE.md already makes SDD the default executor for any written plan, and this repo
  has a [38;5;153mdraft auth-system plan[39m commit. Say the word and I'll start against that plan.

